DESCRIPTION:Sadie Hawkins Day is observed on November 13 in the United Stat
 es\, and it began as a running gag in a comic strip. Al Capp introduced it
  in Li'l Abner in 1937 as an annual event in the invented town of Dogpatch
 \, where the unmarried women were licensed for one day to chase down the b
 achelors\, and the Library of Congress — which holds Capp's original dra
 wings — says it "quickly became a national institution." What it did not
  have\, for most of its life\, was a fixed date.\n\nhttps://todaycelebrate
 s.com/holiday/sadie-hawkins-day/
